             balances[_to] += _value;
             Transfer(msg.sender, _to, _value);
             return true;
         } else { return false; }
     }
     ```
   - Vulnerability: The code does not check if the sum of `balances[msg.sender]` and `_value` exceeds the maximum value of `uint256`. This can lead to an integer overflow, where the value of `balances[msg.sender]` becomes negative after subtracting `_value`.
   - Reason: The code assumes that the subtraction of `_value` from `balances[msg.sender]` will always result in a non-negative value. However, if `_value` is greater than `balances[msg.sender]`, the subtraction will result in a negative value, leading to an integer overflow.

